.Dd April 22, 2026
.Dt CC 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm cc
.Nd Substrate C compiler driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op options
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
compiles C sources, runs the preprocessor, emits assembly/object output, and
links via
.Xr as 1
and
.Xr ld 1 .
.Pp
When invoked as
.Nm cpp ,
preprocessor-only mode is selected.
.Pp
.Dv __BITINT_MAXWIDTH__
is 65535:
.Vt _BitInt Ns Pq Ar N
of any width up to it, and
.Li wb
and
.Li uwb
constants of any size, are laid out and passed as gcc does, with
multiplication, division and the floating conversions done by
libgcc's
.Fn __mulbitint3 ,
.Fn __divmodbitint4 ,
.Fn __floatbitint*
and
.Fn __fix*bitint .
.Vt __int128
and
.Vt unsigned __int128
exist on x86-64, where
.Dv __SIZEOF_INT128__
is 16; on i386 they are rejected and
.Dv __SIZEOF_INT128__
is left undefined, as gcc does.
.Pp
Vector types, GNU
.Sq Li vector_size
and clang's
.Sq Li ext_vector_type ,
are laid out, operated on element by element, and passed and returned
as gcc (and clang) do: on i386 a 16-byte vector travels in
.Li %xmm0
to
.Li %xmm2
and an 8-byte one in an MMX register, so code that calls gcc-built
functions taking 8-byte vectors must not rely on the x87 until the
caller has issued
.Li emms ,
as
.Nm
does.
.Pp
.Vt _Decimal32 ,
.Vt _Decimal64
and
.Vt _Decimal128
hold the BID encoding gcc uses, and their arithmetic and conversions
call libgcc's
.Fn __bid_*
functions, so a program using them links only against a libgcc built
with decimal floating point (a Linux host's is; substrate's is not).
.Pp
Installed host-runnable copies of
.Nm ,
.Xr as 1 ,
and
.Xr ld 1
are typically staged with
.Dq Li make host_dist
and installed with
.Dq Li sudo make HOST_DIST_PREFIX=/opt/substrate host_install .
See
.Xr host_toolchain 7
for the full install and
.Ev PATH
workflow.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-pedantic-errors"
.It Fl E
Preprocess only.
.It Fl S
Compile to assembly.
.It Fl c
Compile and/or assemble only, do not link.
.It Fl o Ar file
Set output path.
With
.Fl E
or
.Fl S ,
a
.Ar file
of
.Ql -
is standard output; with
.Fl c
or when linking it is a file named
.Ql - ,
as with
.Xr gcc 1 .
.It Fl I Ar dir , Fl D Ar name Ns Op =value , Fl U Ar name
Preprocessor include/macro controls.
.It Fl idirafter Ar dir
Add a late include search path.
.It Fl include Ar file , Fl imacros Ar file
Forced include/macro inputs.
.It Fl P
Suppress line markers in preprocessor output.
.It Fl trigraphs
Replace trigraphs
.Pq Ql ??=
for
.Ql #
and so on.
As with
.Xr gcc 1 ,
they are replaced by default only in the ISO modes before C23
.Pq Fl std Ns = Ns Ar c99 , not Ar gnu99 .
.It Fl dM
Dump macro definitions.
.It Fl M , Fl MM , Fl MD , Fl MMD
Emit dependency rules.
.It Fl MF Ar file , Fl MT Ar target , Fl MQ Ar target
Dependency output target controls.
.It Fl std Ns = Ns Ar c90|c95|c99|c11|c17|c23
Language mode.
.Dv __STDC_VERSION__
is not defined in C90 (as the standard has it), and is 199409L for
.Ar iso9899:199409 .
.It Fl ansi
The same as
.Fl std Ns = Ns Ar c89 .
.It Fl O0 , Fl O1 , Fl O2 , Fl O3 , Fl O
Optimization level.
.Fl O
alone is
.Fl O1 ,
as in
.Xr gcc 1 .
Every level above 0 currently runs the same passes.
.It Fl m32 , Fl m64
Target i386 or x86_64 ABI.
The default is the ABI
.Nm
was itself built for: x86_64 on a 64-bit system, i386 on a 32-bit one.
The target's runtime is used: startup code from
.Pa /usr/lib
or
.Pa /usr/lib64 ,
the C library from
.Pa /lib
or
.Pa /lib64 ,
and
.Pa /sbin/ld.so
or
.Pa /sbin/ld64.so
as the program's interpreter.
A 64-bit program is linked as a position-independent executable; a
32-bit one is not, as the i386 code generator writes position-dependent
code.
.It Fl g
Emit debug information.
.It Fl Wall , Fl Werror
Warning controls.
.It Fl pedantic , Fl pedantic-errors
Standards conformance diagnostics.
.It Fl fPIC
Generate position-independent code.
.It Fl fgnu89-inline , Fl fno-gnu89-inline
Use, or do not use, GNU89 inline semantics, the reverse of C99's: a
plain
.Ic inline
function definition is an external definition, and an
.Ic extern inline
one is for inlining only and defines no external symbol.
.Nm
does not inline; it emits an inline-only definition as a local copy.
.It Fl shared
Link shared object.
.It Fl pthread
Enable pthread compile/link behavior.
.It Fl emit-ssa
Validate input textual IR via
.Xr ir-verifier 1 .
.It Fl v
Verbose tool invocation.
.It Fl ###
Print pipeline commands without executing.
.It Fl -bootstrap-gcc
Temporary C-to-assembly fallback via host gcc.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
If a tool
.Nm
runs
.Pq Xr as 1 , Xr ld 1
cannot be executed, or is killed by a signal,
.Nm
says so and exits non-zero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr as 1 ,
.Xr cpp 1 ,
.Xr ir-diff 1 ,
.Xr ir-normalize 1 ,
.Xr ir-verifier 1 ,
.Xr ld 1 ,
.Xr host_toolchain 7
